=== Step 2: your choices ===
  [ok] model: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next

  1) Q2_0     2-bit, the fastest; download 66 GB, uses ~34 GB of RAM
  2) IQ2_XS   2-bit i-quant, a little better quality, close in speed; download 68 GB, uses ~36 GB of RAM
  3) IQ3_XXS  3-bit i-quant, better quality, slower (more CPU work per token); download 76 GB, uses ~43 GB of RAM
  4) IQ3_S    (recommended) 3.5-bit i-quant, the best quality (matches the full model), the slowest; needs a 64 GB PC with little else running; download 84 GB, uses ~50 GB of RAM
  [ok] size: IQ2_XS

  Context length = how much text the model can see at once (your chat, files, tool output).
  Longer needs more VRAM for it, so fewer experts fit on the GPU:
  1) 8K tokens
  2) 32K tokens
  3) 64K tokens
  4) 128K tokens   (recommended for your GPU)
  5) 200K tokens
  6) 256K tokens
  7) 384K tokens   (experimental: setup adds rope scaling)
  8) 512K tokens   (experimental: setup adds rope scaling)
  [ok] context: 131072 tokens
  [ok] KV cache: 8-bit
  [ok] images: on

  EXPERIMENTAL - speed projection: a small control vector applied while the model runs (layers 4-44).
